        "colorIndex": 7,
        "text": "You are a bioinformatics expert performing literature mining.\n\nWe have a **confirmed kinase-substrate pair** from a scientific paper, but the **phosphorylation site was not mentioned in the abstract**. Your job is to find it in the **full text**.\n\nArticle title: {title}\n\nKinase: {enzyme}\nSubstrate: {substrate}\n\nBelow is the relevant full text of the article.\n\n---\n{fulltext}\n---\n\nIdentify the **specific residue(s) on the substrate that are phosphorylated by the kinase**.\n\nReturn only residues on the **given substrate**.\n\n## Search Strategy\n\n### 1. Direct statements (strongest evidence)\n\"X phosphorylates Y at Ser301\", \"phosphorylation of Y at Tyr-397 by X\", \"X adds phosphate to Thr287 of Y\", \"X-mediated phosphorylation of Y occurs on Ser473\".\n\n### 2. Site-specific phosphorylation combined with kinase action\nSometimes the paper states the phosphorylation site on the substrate, and separately that the kinase phosphorylates the substrate or is required for that phosphorylation. In such cases, if the article clearly identifies a specific phosphosite on the substrate and shows that the given kinase is responsible for, required for, or directly causes phosphorylation of that substrate, the phosphosite may be treated as the likely phosphorylation site.\n\nDo **not** extract a site merely because it is a known phosphosite of the substrate unless this article links that site to the given kinase.\n\n### 3. Experimental evidence identifying a kinase-linked phosphosite\nSite-specific antibodies (phospho-Tyr397 antibody, pS262 antibody), phosphosite mutants (Y12F, S473A, T308D), phosphopeptides or mass spectrometry, in vitro kinase assays, and phrases describing site positions.\n\n## Residue Formats to Recognize\nFull residue names (Ser301, Thr287, Tyr397), hyphen format (Ser-301, Tyr-397), single-letter format (S301, T287, Y397), phosphorylated notation (pS262, pT217, pY397), mutation notation (Y12F, S473A, T308E), and position descriptions (\"position 12\", \"residue 397\").\n\n## Extraction Rules\n\n1. Extract **only residues on the specified substrate**.\n2. Prefer **direct statements** assigning phosphorylation of the substrate to the given kinase.\n3. Extract sites supported by mutants, phospho-antibodies, phosphopeptides, mass spectrometry, or kinase assays only when the evidence links the site to the given kinase.\n4. If a site is mentioned for the substrate but the article does not connect it to the given kinase, do **not** extract it.\n5. If multiple sites are reported, return them as a **semicolon-separated string**.\n6. If no site can be identified, return **null**.\n7. Use **only information from this article** (no external knowledge).\n8. In evidence_texts, include the **verbatim sentences** (exact quotes) that mention the site. In reasoning, briefly explain how they support the extraction.\n\n## Output Format\nReturn a valid JSON object with phosphosite, reasoning, evidence_texts (list of verbatim sentences), and confidence (0-1).",
