n descriptions (\"position 12\", \"residue 397\").\n\n## Extraction Rules\n\n1. Extract **only residues on the specified substrate**.\n2. Prefer **direct statements** assigning phosphorylation of the substrate to the given kinase.\n3. Extract sites supported by mutants, phospho-antibodies, phosphopeptides, mass spectrometry, or kinase assays only when the evidence links the site to the given kinase.\n4. If a site is mentioned for the substrate but the article does not connect it to the given kinase, do **not** extract it.\n5. If multiple sites are reported, return them as a **semicolon-separated string**.\n6. If no site can be identified, return **null**.\n7. Use **only information from this article** (no external knowledge).\n8. In evidence_texts, include the **verbatim sentences** (exact quotes) that mention the site. In reasoning, briefly explain how they support the extraction.\n\n## Output Format\nReturn a valid JSON object with phosphosite, reasoning, evidence_texts (list of verbatim sentences), and confidence (0-1)."
